      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/119/5533",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَمِيرُ اَلْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"اَلْمَرْأَةُ لاَ يُوصَى إِلَيْهَا لِأَنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَقُولُ ۝ وَ لاٰ تُؤْتُوا اَلسُّفَهٰاءَ أَمْوٰالَكُمُ ۝."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5533 - Al-Sakuni narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) from his father, Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), from his forefathers, peace be upon them, who said that the Commander of the Faithful (as) said:\n\"A woman should not be appointed as an executor of a will because Allah (swt), the Almighty and Glorious, says: \"And do not give the weak-minded your wealth\" (Surah An-Nisa 4:5).\""
        ]
      }
    },
